Also, I wanted to understand why for some filetypes, I get N/C/V/I/R for the different modes, while for others I get the modes in complete words.

It does not depend on filetype, but on the total width of the window. That content comes from section_mode(): one letter is a short form and full word is a full form. Short form is shown if window's width is less than trunc_width argument (which in default active content is 120).

Thank you! I see, so it is possible to change this default, from 120 to 100? I have this as my setup.

